1
00:00:32,080 --> 00:00:35,920
You're wondering why I brought you all here.

2
00:00:36,060 --> 00:00:39,460
After all, we just had a feast.

3
00:00:39,760 --> 00:00:42,180
Since when does old Walder

4
00:00:42,180 --> 00:00:45,670
give us two feasts in a single fortnight?

5
00:00:47,850 --> 00:00:50,740
Well, it's no good being Lord of the Riverlands

6
00:00:50,740 --> 00:00:53,110
if you can't celebrate with your family.

7
00:00:53,110 --> 00:00:54,740
That's what I say!

8
00:00:54,760 --> 00:00:58,420
Yes!

9
00:01:02,040 --> 00:01:06,120
I've gathered every Frey who means a damn thing

10
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:10,370
so I can tell you my plans for this great house

11
00:01:10,560 --> 00:01:13,070
now that winter has come.

12
00:01:14,080 --> 00:01:17,480
But first, a toast!

13
00:01:18,750 --> 00:01:21,910
No more of that Dornish horse piss!

14
00:01:22,360 --> 00:01:25,200
This is the finest Arbor gold!

15
00:01:25,380 --> 00:01:28,570
Proper wine for proper heroes!

16
00:01:33,630 --> 00:01:35,700
Stand together!

17
00:01:35,760 --> 00:01:37,610
Stand together!

18
00:01:46,960 --> 00:01:47,960
Not you.

19
00:01:48,270 --> 00:01:51,370
I'm not wasting good wine on a damn woman.

20
00:01:54,740 --> 00:01:58,750
Maybe I'm not the most pleasant man.

21
00:01:59,130 --> 00:02:02,620
I'll admit it. But I'm proud of you lot.

22
00:02:02,630 --> 00:02:05,630
You're my family, the men who helped me

23
00:02:05,630 --> 00:02:08,840
slaughter the Starks at the Red Wedding.

24
00:02:09,890 --> 00:02:13,100
Yes, yes.

25
00:02:13,480 --> 00:02:14,640
Cheer.

26
00:02:15,660 --> 00:02:18,570
Brave men, all of you.

27
00:02:19,080 --> 00:02:22,490
Butchered a woman pregnant with her babe.

28
00:02:23,410 --> 00:02:26,800
Cut the throat of a mother of five.

29
00:02:28,470 --> 00:02:33,270
Slaughtered your guests after inviting them into your home.

30
00:02:34,930 --> 00:02:40,690
But you didn't slaughter every one of the Starks.

31
00:02:41,520 --> 00:02:44,940
No, no, that was your mistake.

32
00:02:45,300 --> 00:02:49,250
You should have ripped them all out, root and stem.

33
00:02:55,750 --> 00:02:57,950
Leave one wolf alive

34
00:02:57,950 --> 00:03:00,450
and the sheep are never safe.

35
00:03:26,500 --> 00:03:28,440
When people ask you what happened here...

36
00:03:29,880 --> 00:03:31,830
tell them the North remembers.

37
00:03:33,260 --> 00:03:37,000
Tell them winter came for House Frey.

38
00:07:59,520 --> 00:08:01,010
You wildlings?

39
00:08:01,270 --> 00:08:04,420
I'm Meera Reed, daughter of Howland Reed.

40
00:08:06,100 --> 00:08:07,750
This is Brandon Stark,

41
00:08:08,240 --> 00:08:09,820
son of Ned Stark.

42
00:08:14,150 --> 00:08:15,800
How do I know that's true?

43
00:08:19,200 --> 00:08:21,180
You were at the Fist of the First Men.

44
00:08:22,620 --> 00:08:23,990
You were at Hardhome.

45
00:08:25,990 --> 00:08:27,990
You've seen the Army of the Dead.

46
00:08:29,580 --> 00:08:31,070
You've seen the Night King.

47
00:08:31,870 --> 00:08:33,240
He's coming for us.

48
00:08:34,980 --> 00:08:36,200
For all of us.

49
00:08:44,250 --> 00:08:45,210
Okay, come on.

50
00:08:46,340 --> 00:08:47,680
Let's get them inside.

51
00:09:17,260 --> 00:09:20,450
I want every northern maester to scour their records

52
00:09:20,460 --> 00:09:22,890
for any mention of dragonglass.

53
00:09:23,760 --> 00:09:25,640
Dragonglass kills white walkers.

54
00:09:25,640 --> 00:09:28,010
It's more valuable to us now than gold.

55
00:09:28,300 --> 00:09:29,930
We need to find it, we need to mine it,

56
00:09:29,940 --> 00:09:31,840
we need to make weapons from it.

57
00:09:33,100 --> 00:09:35,850
Everyone aged 10 to 60

58
00:09:36,120 --> 00:09:39,450
will drill daily with spears, pikes, bow and arrow.

59
00:09:39,450 --> 00:09:42,770
It's about time we taught these boys of summer how to fight.

60
00:09:43,540 --> 00:09:44,890
Not just the boys.

61
00:09:45,520 --> 00:09:47,210
We can't defend the North

62
00:09:47,340 --> 00:09:49,700
if only half the population is fighting.

63
00:09:50,360 --> 00:09:54,610
You expect me to put a spear in my granddaughter's hand?

64
00:09:54,880 --> 00:09:58,100
I don't plan on knitting by the fire while men fight for me.

65
00:09:58,100 --> 00:10:01,070
I might be small, Lord Glover, and I might be a girl,

66
00:10:01,070 --> 00:10:03,720
but I am every bit as much a Northerner as you.

67
00:10:03,720 --> 00:10:05,080
Indeed you are, my lady. No one has questioned--

68
00:10:05,080 --> 00:10:07,610
And I don't need your permission to defend the North.

69
00:10:10,550 --> 00:10:11,860
We'll begin training every man,

70
00:10:11,860 --> 00:10:15,050
woman, boy, and girl on Bear Island.

71
00:10:15,320 --> 00:10:16,400
Aye!

72
00:10:17,350 --> 00:10:18,620
While we're preparing for attack,

73
00:10:18,630 --> 00:10:20,310
we need to shore up our defenses.

74
00:10:21,290 --> 00:10:22,220
The only thing standing

75
00:10:22,220 --> 00:10:24,600
between us and the Army of the Dead is the Wall,

76
00:10:24,600 --> 00:10:27,830
and the Wall hasn't been properly manned in centuries.

77
00:10:28,610 --> 00:10:30,900
I'm not the king of the Free Folk.

78
00:10:32,710 --> 00:10:35,010
But if we're going to survive this winter together...

79
00:10:36,410 --> 00:10:39,040
You want us to man the castles for you?

80
00:10:39,520 --> 00:10:40,320
Aye.

81
00:10:40,760 --> 00:10:43,310
Last time we saw the Night King was at Hardhome.

82
00:10:43,540 --> 00:10:46,660
The closest castle to Hardhome is Eastwatch-by-the-Sea.

83
00:10:46,660 --> 00:10:48,490
Then that's where I'll go.

84
00:10:48,740 --> 00:10:51,330
Looks like we're the Night's Watch now.

85
00:10:53,510 --> 00:10:55,220
If they breach the Wall,

86
00:10:55,220 --> 00:10:56,910
the first two castles in their path

87
00:10:56,910 --> 00:10:59,280
are Last Hearth and Karhold.

88
00:10:59,420 --> 00:11:02,680
The Umbers and the Karstarks betrayed the North.

89
00:11:03,080 --> 00:11:04,710
Their castles should be torn down

90
00:11:04,710 --> 00:11:06,520
with not a stone left standing.

91
00:11:06,520 --> 00:11:09,040
The castles committed no crimes.

92
00:11:09,220 --> 00:11:12,550
And we need every fortress we have for the war to come.

93
00:11:12,550 --> 00:11:15,780
We should give the Last Hearth and Karhold to new families,

94
00:11:15,780 --> 00:11:18,670
loyal families who supported us against Ramsay.

95
00:11:18,690 --> 00:11:20,460
Aye!

96
00:11:22,360 --> 00:11:24,020
The Umbers and the Karstarks

97
00:11:24,020 --> 00:11:26,390
have fought beside the Starks for centuries.

98
00:11:26,390 --> 00:11:28,950
They've kept faith for generation after generation.

99
00:11:28,950 --> 00:11:30,520
And then they broke faith.

100
00:11:30,520 --> 00:11:33,500
I'm not going to strip these families of their ancestral homes

101
00:11:33,500 --> 00:11:35,990
because of the crimes of a few reckless sons.

102
00:11:35,990 --> 00:11:37,730
So there's no punishment for treason

103
00:11:37,730 --> 00:11:39,740
and no reward for loyalty?

104
00:11:45,490 --> 00:11:47,620
The punishment for treason is death.

105
00:11:48,450 --> 00:11:51,020
Smalljon Umber died on the field of battle.

106
00:11:51,020 --> 00:11:53,810
Harald Karstark died on the field of battle.

107
00:11:53,810 --> 00:11:56,180
They died fighting for Ramsay.

108
00:11:56,260 --> 00:11:57,780
Give the castles to the families

109
00:11:57,780 --> 00:12:00,380
of the men who died fighting for you.

110
00:12:13,450 --> 00:12:16,330
When I was Lord Commander of the Night's Watch...

111
00:12:17,850 --> 00:12:20,110
I executed men who betrayed me.

112
00:12:20,620 --> 00:12:23,940
I executed men who refused to follow orders.

113
00:12:24,290 --> 00:12:26,020
My father always said,

114
00:12:26,280 --> 00:12:28,760
"The man who passes the sentence should swing the sword,"

115
00:12:28,760 --> 00:12:31,490
and I have tried to live by those words.

116
00:12:32,170 --> 00:12:35,420
But I will not punish a son for his father's sins,

117
00:12:35,520 --> 00:12:37,670
and I will not take a family home

118
00:12:37,670 --> 00:12:41,000
away from a family it has belonged to for centuries.

119
00:12:41,420 --> 00:12:43,280
That is my decision,

120
00:12:43,910 --> 00:12:46,180
and my decision is final.

121
00:12:52,700 --> 00:12:53,800
Ned Umber.

122
00:13:01,710 --> 00:13:03,330
Alys Karstark.

123
00:13:18,210 --> 00:13:19,960
For centuries, our families fought

124
00:13:19,960 --> 00:13:22,010
side by side on the battlefield.

125
00:13:22,850 --> 00:13:27,280
I ask you to pledge your loyalty once again to House Stark,

126
00:13:27,840 --> 00:13:29,910
to serve as our bannermen

127
00:13:30,370 --> 00:13:33,420
and come to our aid whenever called upon.

128
00:13:41,940 --> 00:13:42,870
Stand.

129
00:13:46,670 --> 00:13:49,030
Yesterday's wars don't matter anymore.

130
00:13:49,660 --> 00:13:52,100
The North needs to band together,

131
00:13:52,330 --> 00:13:54,430
all the living north.

132
00:13:55,270 --> 00:13:57,930
Will you stand beside me, Ned and Alys,

133
00:13:57,940 --> 00:13:59,780
now and always?

134
00:13:59,780 --> 00:14:02,050
Now and always!

135
00:14:21,480 --> 00:14:23,700
You are my sister, but I am king now.

136
00:14:23,790 --> 00:14:25,250
Will you start wearing a crown?

137
00:14:25,250 --> 00:14:26,600
When you question my decisions

138
00:14:26,600 --> 00:14:29,070
in front of the other lords and ladies, you undermine me.

139
00:14:29,070 --> 00:14:30,940
So I can't question your decisions anymore?

140
00:14:30,940 --> 00:14:31,860
Of course you can, but--

141
00:14:31,860 --> 00:14:33,950
Joffrey never let anyone question his authority.

142
00:14:33,950 --> 00:14:35,600
You think he was a good king?

143
00:14:38,050 --> 00:14:39,580
Do you think I'm Joffrey?

144
00:14:43,540 --> 00:14:46,200
You're as far from Joffrey as anyone I've ever met.

145
00:14:46,490 --> 00:14:47,430
Thank you.

146
00:14:49,950 --> 00:14:51,280
You're good at this, you know.

147
00:14:51,280 --> 00:14:53,320
- At what? - At ruling.

148
00:14:54,990 --> 00:14:55,700
No.

149
00:14:55,720 --> 00:14:56,630
You are.

150
00:14:57,500 --> 00:14:58,430
You are.

151
00:15:01,130 --> 00:15:02,940
They respect you, they really do,

152
00:15:02,940 --> 00:15:04,110
but you have to

153
00:15:05,190 --> 00:15:06,470
Why are you laughing?

154
00:15:07,500 --> 00:15:08,740
What did father used to say?

155
00:15:08,740 --> 00:15:11,810
Everything before the word "But" is horse shit.

156
00:15:12,210 --> 00:15:13,510
He never said that to me.

157
00:15:13,520 --> 00:15:16,410
No. No, he never cursed in front of his girls.

158
00:15:16,410 --> 00:15:18,500
Because he was trying to protect us.

159
00:15:19,510 --> 00:15:22,360
He never wanted us to see how dirty the world really is,

160
00:15:22,360 --> 00:15:25,290
but Father couldn't protect me and neither can you.

161
00:15:25,340 --> 00:15:27,760
- Stop trying. - All right, I'll stop trying to protect you

162
00:15:27,760 --> 00:15:29,150
and you stop trying to undermine me.

163
00:15:29,150 --> 00:15:31,010
I'm not trying to undermine you!

164
00:15:33,010 --> 00:15:35,520
You have to be smarter than Father.

165
00:15:36,160 --> 00:15:37,940
You need to be smarter than Robb.

166
00:15:38,780 --> 00:15:40,310
I loved them, I miss them,

167
00:15:40,320 --> 00:15:41,620
but they made stupid mistakes,

168
00:15:41,620 --> 00:15:43,740
and they both lost their heads for it.

169
00:15:43,740 --> 00:15:45,500
And how should I be smarter?

170
00:15:45,970 --> 00:15:47,360
By listening to you?

171
00:15:49,540 --> 00:15:50,980
Would that be so terrible?

172
00:15:52,610 --> 00:15:55,770
A raven from King's Landing, Your Grace.

173
00:16:05,510 --> 00:16:07,790
"Cersei of House Lannister, First of Her Name,

174
00:16:07,790 --> 00:16:09,840
Queen of the Andals and the First Men,

175
00:16:09,840 --> 00:16:11,320
Protector of the Seven Kingdoms--"

176
00:16:11,320 --> 00:16:12,560
What does she want?

177
00:16:14,930 --> 00:16:16,400
Come to King's Landing.

178
00:16:16,910 --> 00:16:20,010
Bend the knee or suffer the fate of all traitors.

179
00:16:20,870 --> 00:16:22,820
You've been so consumed with the enemy to the north,

180
00:16:22,820 --> 00:16:24,800
you've forgotten about the one to the south.

181
00:16:24,800 --> 00:16:27,280
I'm consumed with the Night King because I've seen him.

182
00:16:27,720 --> 00:16:29,980
And believe me, you'd think of little else if you had, too.

183
00:16:29,980 --> 00:16:31,910
We still have a wall between us and the Night King.

184
00:16:31,910 --> 00:16:33,840
There's nothing between us and Cersei.

185
00:16:33,840 --> 00:16:36,530
There's a thousand miles between us and Cersei.

186
00:16:36,770 --> 00:16:39,430
Winter is here. The Lannisters are a southern army.

187
00:16:39,510 --> 00:16:41,290
They've never ranged this far north.

188
00:16:41,290 --> 00:16:43,780
You're the military man, but I know her.

189
00:16:44,480 --> 00:16:47,730
If you're her enemy, she'll never stop until she's destroyed you.

190
00:16:47,730 --> 00:16:51,060
Everyone who's ever crossed her, she's found a way to murder.

191
00:16:53,970 --> 00:16:56,050
You almost sound as if you admire her.

192
00:16:59,790 --> 00:17:01,650
I learned a great deal from her.

193
00:17:38,410 --> 00:17:39,730
What is this?

194
00:17:40,600 --> 00:17:42,840
It's what we've been waiting for our whole lives.

195
00:17:43,060 --> 00:17:45,640
It's what Father trained us for, whether he knew it or not.

196
00:17:45,640 --> 00:17:46,690
He knew it.

197
00:17:47,330 --> 00:17:49,140
Made me memorize every damn city, town,

198
00:17:49,140 --> 00:17:50,760
lake, forest, and mountain.

199
00:17:50,760 --> 00:17:53,140
It's ours now. We just have to take it.

200
00:17:54,650 --> 00:17:56,590
You've been quiet since you came home.

201
00:17:57,170 --> 00:17:58,180
Are you angry with me?

202
00:17:58,180 --> 00:18:00,170
No, not angry.

203
00:18:01,620 --> 00:18:02,860
Are you afraid of me?

204
00:18:04,820 --> 00:18:05,950
Should I be?

205
00:18:09,920 --> 00:18:13,070
Daenerys Targaryen has chosen Tyrion to be her Hand.

206
00:18:13,720 --> 00:18:16,210
Right now, they're sailing across the Narrow Sea,

207
00:18:16,420 --> 00:18:18,870
hoping to take back her father's throne.

208
00:18:19,380 --> 00:18:20,570
Our little brother,

209
00:18:21,790 --> 00:18:23,890
the one you love so much,

210
00:18:24,010 --> 00:18:25,200
the one you set free,

211
00:18:25,860 --> 00:18:28,670
the one who murdered our father and our first-born son,

212
00:18:29,090 --> 00:18:32,330
now he stands beside our enemies and gives them counsel.

213
00:18:36,140 --> 00:18:38,690
He's out there somewhere at the head of an armada.

214
00:18:40,290 --> 00:18:41,680
Where will they land?

215
00:18:44,480 --> 00:18:45,910
Dragonstone.

216
00:18:46,500 --> 00:18:48,710
They have deep-water ports for the ships.

217
00:18:48,710 --> 00:18:50,660
Stannis left the castle unoccupied,

218
00:18:50,670 --> 00:18:52,230
and that's where she was born.

219
00:18:52,910 --> 00:18:54,420
Enemies to the east.

220
00:18:54,810 --> 00:18:56,170
Enemies to the south--

221
00:18:56,170 --> 00:18:58,980
Ellaria Sand and her brood of bitches.

222
00:18:58,980 --> 00:19:00,510
Enemies to the west--

223
00:19:01,010 --> 00:19:02,870
Olenna, the old cunt.

224
00:19:02,870 --> 00:19:04,050
Another traitor.

225
00:19:06,380 --> 00:19:07,980
Enemies to the north.

226
00:19:08,430 --> 00:19:10,890
Ned Stark's bastard has been named King in the North

227
00:19:10,890 --> 00:19:14,290
and that murdering whore Sansa stands beside him.

228
00:19:14,600 --> 00:19:17,120
Enemies everywhere. We're surrounded by traitors.

229
00:19:17,130 --> 00:19:18,620
You're in command of the Lannister army now.

230
00:19:18,620 --> 00:19:21,040
- How do we proceed? - Winter is here.

231
00:19:22,080 --> 00:19:25,730
We can't win a war if we can't feed our men and our horses.

232
00:19:25,950 --> 00:19:29,200
The Tyrells have the grain, the Tyrells have the livestock.

233
00:19:29,480 --> 00:19:31,420
Will the Tyrell bannermen stand alongside

234
00:19:31,420 --> 00:19:34,690
a Dothraki horde and Unsullied slave soldiers?

235
00:19:34,690 --> 00:19:37,000
If they think Daenerys will win.

236
00:19:37,340 --> 00:19:39,510
No one wants to fight on the losing side.

237
00:19:39,510 --> 00:19:42,860
Right now, we look like the losing side.

238
00:19:43,950 --> 00:19:45,270
I'm the Queen of the Seven Kingdoms.

239
00:19:45,270 --> 00:19:47,600
Three kingdoms, at best.

240
00:19:48,700 --> 00:19:50,810
I'm not sure you understand how much danger we're in.

241
00:19:50,810 --> 00:19:52,500
I understand we're in a war for survival.

242
00:19:52,500 --> 00:19:54,640
I understand whoever loses dies.

243
00:19:55,860 --> 00:19:57,450
I understand whoever wins could launch a dynasty

244
00:19:57,450 --> 00:19:59,170
that lasts a thousand years.

245
00:19:59,170 --> 00:20:00,900
A dynasty for whom?

246
00:20:02,230 --> 00:20:04,320
Our children are dead.

247
00:20:05,330 --> 00:20:06,930
We're the last of us.

248
00:20:07,330 --> 00:20:08,770
A dynasty for us, then.

249
00:20:11,710 --> 00:20:13,640
We never talked about Tommen.

250
00:20:16,560 --> 00:20:17,990
There's nothing to say.

251
00:20:18,260 --> 00:20:20,320
Our baby boy killed himself.

252
00:20:20,320 --> 00:20:21,500
He betrayed me.

253
00:20:21,780 --> 00:20:23,360
He betrayed us both.

254
00:20:23,500 --> 00:20:25,100
Should we spend our days mourning the dead--

255
00:20:25,100 --> 00:20:26,830
mother, father, and all our children?

256
00:20:26,830 --> 00:20:28,950
- Cersei-- - I loved them. I did.

257
00:20:29,590 --> 00:20:32,100
But they're ashes now and we're still flesh and blood.

258
00:20:32,590 --> 00:20:35,330
We're the last Lannisters, the last ones who count.

259
00:20:41,290 --> 00:20:43,790
Even Lannisters can't survive without allies.

260
00:20:43,790 --> 00:20:45,870
Where are our allies now?

261
00:20:47,220 --> 00:20:49,430
You saw what happened to Walder Frey and his family.

262
00:20:49,430 --> 00:20:50,540
I heard.

263
00:20:50,930 --> 00:20:53,450
- How could we ever trust a man like that? - We couldn't.

264
00:20:53,450 --> 00:20:55,260
He was a useless, old coward,

265
00:20:55,260 --> 00:20:57,470
but the Freys supported us.

266
00:20:57,830 --> 00:20:58,550
Now they're all dead.

267
00:20:58,550 --> 00:21:00,190
Whoever killed them is no friend of ours.

268
00:21:00,200 --> 00:21:01,890
We need allies.

269
00:21:01,910 --> 00:21:03,610
Stronger, better allies.

270
00:21:03,620 --> 00:21:05,390
We can't win this war alone.

271
00:21:08,090 --> 00:21:10,320
You think I listened to Father for 40 years

272
00:21:10,320 --> 00:21:11,300
and learned nothing?

273
00:21:48,520 --> 00:21:50,000
The Greyjoys?

274
00:21:50,100 --> 00:21:52,570
You invited the Greyjoys to King's Landing?

275
00:21:52,570 --> 00:21:54,950
- Not all of them. - Well, it looks like all of them.

276
00:21:55,370 --> 00:21:56,610
I invited Euron Greyjoy,

277
00:21:56,610 --> 00:21:58,870
the new King of the Iron Islands.

278
00:21:59,520 --> 00:22:02,440
You said yourself we needed stronger, better allies.

279
00:22:02,690 --> 00:22:05,180
- There you are. - How are they better allies?

280
00:22:05,180 --> 00:22:07,500
How are they different from the Freys?

281
00:22:07,720 --> 00:22:08,810
They both broke their promises

282
00:22:08,810 --> 00:22:11,670
and murdered their former friends as soon as it suited them.

283
00:22:11,670 --> 00:22:14,390
So does everyone when it suits them.

284
00:22:14,600 --> 00:22:17,130
Unlike the Freys, they have ships.

285
00:22:17,290 --> 00:22:20,010
- And they're good at killing. - They're not good at anything.

286
00:22:20,010 --> 00:22:23,380
I know the ironborn. They're bitter, angry little people.

287
00:22:23,450 --> 00:22:24,150
All they know how to do is

288
00:22:24,150 --> 00:22:26,740
steal things they can't build or grow themselves.

289
00:22:26,740 --> 00:22:28,540
Euron Greyjoy didn't come here for that.

290
00:22:28,550 --> 00:22:30,490
Oh, what did he come here for, then?

291
00:22:31,010 --> 00:22:32,270
A queen.

292
00:22:45,360 --> 00:22:47,940
The moment I was chosen Lord of the Iron Islands,

293
00:22:48,330 --> 00:22:49,580
they turned on me.

294
00:22:50,560 --> 00:22:51,740
Their own uncle.

295
00:22:51,930 --> 00:22:53,910
They stole my best ships and ran.

296
00:22:54,960 --> 00:22:56,600
Sailed them right across the world

297
00:22:56,600 --> 00:22:58,600
and gave them to the Dragon Queen

298
00:22:58,600 --> 00:23:01,930
so she could bring her armies here to attack you.

299
00:23:03,290 --> 00:23:05,880
It's nothing compared to the treason you suffered

300
00:23:05,880 --> 00:23:09,480
at the hands of a family member, from what I hear.

301
00:23:09,480 --> 00:23:12,100
But still, it bothers me.

302
00:23:14,010 --> 00:23:16,530
Murdering them would make me feel a lot better.

303
00:23:17,170 --> 00:23:20,890
And since it appears that all our treasonous family members

304
00:23:20,890 --> 00:23:23,000
are fighting for the same side,

305
00:23:23,340 --> 00:23:25,370
I thought we rightful monarchs

306
00:23:26,090 --> 00:23:27,680
could murder them together.

307
00:23:34,390 --> 00:23:37,250
You're not a rightful monarch, though, are you?

308
00:23:41,180 --> 00:23:42,450
The Greyjoys rebelled against

309
00:23:42,450 --> 00:23:43,990
the throne for the right to be monarchs,

310
00:23:43,990 --> 00:23:47,640
but as I recall, you were soundly defeated.

311
00:23:48,110 --> 00:23:49,290
Come to mention it,

312
00:23:49,960 --> 00:23:52,390
weren't you the one who started that rebellion

313
00:23:52,390 --> 00:23:56,030
by sailing to Casterly Rock and burning the Lannister fleet?

314
00:23:56,670 --> 00:23:58,450
You certainly caught us there.

315
00:23:58,680 --> 00:24:01,000
Very smart move on your part.

316
00:24:01,250 --> 00:24:04,450
Of course, we all made it to the Iron Islands anyway.

317
00:24:05,370 --> 00:24:06,440
I was there.

318
00:24:06,500 --> 00:24:08,010
I remember very well.

319
00:24:08,340 --> 00:24:09,360
I saw you.

320
00:24:09,790 --> 00:24:11,550
I heard so much talk.

321
00:24:12,310 --> 00:24:14,860
The best in the world. No one can stop him.

322
00:24:15,590 --> 00:24:17,460
I didn't believe it, to be honest.

323
00:24:18,010 --> 00:24:20,630
But I must say when you rushed through the breach

324
00:24:20,630 --> 00:24:22,770
and started cutting people down...

325
00:24:26,400 --> 00:24:28,300
it was glorious.

326
00:24:28,400 --> 00:24:29,800
Like a dance.

327
00:24:29,800 --> 00:24:32,830
The people I was cutting down were your own kin.

328
00:24:32,830 --> 00:24:34,370
The place was getting crowded.

329
00:24:35,340 --> 00:24:37,610
I enjoyed watching it. I truly did.

330
00:24:37,610 --> 00:24:39,860
And I enjoyed killing Greyjoys.

331
00:24:39,870 --> 00:24:41,260
A good thing for me.

332
00:24:42,610 --> 00:24:45,850
If you hadn't crushed us, I wouldn't have gone into exile.

333
00:24:45,910 --> 00:24:47,280
If I hadn't done that,

334
00:24:47,930 --> 00:24:51,240
I wouldn't be the greatest captain on the 14 seas.

335
00:24:52,500 --> 00:24:53,980
If not the most humble.

336
00:24:55,650 --> 00:24:56,830
You're not humble.

337
00:24:58,720 --> 00:25:01,090
You're the queen of a great nation.

338
00:25:01,890 --> 00:25:03,910
You don't care about the Iron Islands.

339
00:25:03,910 --> 00:25:08,120
They're nothing but rocks and bird shit and--

340
00:25:08,320 --> 00:25:10,840
and a lot of very unattractive people.

341
00:25:11,430 --> 00:25:13,920
The Iron Fleet, on the other hand,

342
00:25:14,130 --> 00:25:16,100
that's something else entirely.

343
00:25:17,090 --> 00:25:20,080
It's the greatest armada Westeros has ever seen.

344
00:25:20,790 --> 00:25:23,690
With the Iron Fleet, you own the seas.

345
00:25:25,020 --> 00:25:27,320
You can defeat the invaders of the east

346
00:25:27,530 --> 00:25:29,940
and the pretenders of the north and south.

347
00:25:30,800 --> 00:25:32,310
What do you want in return?

348
00:25:34,210 --> 00:25:36,110
Ever since I was a little boy,

349
00:25:37,470 --> 00:25:38,990
I wanted to grow up and marry

350
00:25:38,990 --> 00:25:41,390
the most beautiful woman in the world.

351
00:25:42,070 --> 00:25:43,550
So here I am,

352
00:25:43,900 --> 00:25:45,660
with a thousand ships

353
00:25:46,480 --> 00:25:48,060
and two good hands.

354
00:25:53,480 --> 00:25:55,230
I decline your proposal.

355
00:25:57,810 --> 00:25:59,130
Why?

356
00:25:59,140 --> 00:26:00,820
You're not trustworthy.

357
00:26:01,620 --> 00:26:03,570
You've broken promises to allies before

358
00:26:03,580 --> 00:26:06,070
and murdered them at the nearest opportunity.

359
00:26:06,330 --> 00:26:07,750
You murdered your own brother.

360
00:26:08,950 --> 00:26:11,430
You should try it. Feels wonderful.

361
00:26:13,020 --> 00:26:15,040
I don't expect you to trust me outright.

362
00:26:15,040 --> 00:26:17,600
You need proof of my honest intentions.

363
00:26:17,610 --> 00:26:18,960
In my experience,

364
00:26:19,060 --> 00:26:21,820
the surest way to a woman's heart is with a gift.

365
00:26:22,150 --> 00:26:23,400
A priceless gift.

366
00:26:24,180 --> 00:26:26,070
I won't return to King's Landing

367
00:26:26,300 --> 00:26:27,840
until I have that for you.

368
00:29:34,010 --> 00:29:35,990
Ah, Maester Weyland.

369
00:29:37,340 --> 00:29:40,560
A drinker's liver if ever I saw one.

370
00:29:41,800 --> 00:29:42,790
Weigh that.

371
00:29:43,750 --> 00:29:46,440
The triumph of transitory pleasures.

372
00:29:47,210 --> 00:29:49,020
Mankind's curse.

373
00:29:49,020 --> 00:29:52,050
Archmaester, I was wondering...

374
00:29:52,380 --> 00:29:53,460
What's the weight?

375
00:30:00,220 --> 00:30:03,210
I was wondering if you had considered my proposition.

376
00:30:03,490 --> 00:30:05,350
I don't remember your proposition.

377
00:30:06,300 --> 00:30:09,280
I asked you if, in light of what I've seen in the North,

378
00:30:09,460 --> 00:30:12,560
if I could have access to the restricted area of the library.

379
00:30:12,610 --> 00:30:14,050
That area is reserved for maesters.

380
00:30:14,060 --> 00:30:16,060
- Are you a maester? - No.

381
00:30:17,020 --> 00:30:19,020
Not a very strong proposition, is it?

382
00:30:28,130 --> 00:30:30,760
Archmaester, with respect,

383
00:30:31,340 --> 00:30:32,510
I've seen them...

384
00:30:32,790 --> 00:30:34,140
the Army of the Dead.

385
00:30:34,990 --> 00:30:36,320
The white walkers.

386
00:30:38,170 --> 00:30:40,410
I was sent here to learn how to defeat them,

387
00:30:40,490 --> 00:30:42,180
but everyone in the Citadel,

388
00:30:42,510 --> 00:30:44,170
those who will even talk to me,

389
00:30:44,800 --> 00:30:47,670
they all doubt the walkers ever existed in the first place.

390
00:30:48,010 --> 00:30:49,960
Everyone in the Citadel doubts everything.

391
00:30:49,960 --> 00:30:51,020
It's their job.

392
00:30:57,030 --> 00:30:59,920
But the tales of the Long Night can't be pure fabrication.

393
00:31:01,780 --> 00:31:04,480
Too many similarities from unconnected sources.

394
00:31:05,030 --> 00:31:07,120
Sources in the restricted area?

395
00:31:07,120 --> 00:31:08,330
The very same.

396
00:31:10,070 --> 00:31:11,590
And the simplest explanation

397
00:31:11,590 --> 00:31:14,370
for your grating obsession with the white walkers

398
00:31:14,370 --> 00:31:16,130
is that you're telling the truth

399
00:31:16,320 --> 00:31:17,870
and that you saw what you say you saw.

400
00:31:19,220 --> 00:31:22,110
So, you believe me.

401
00:31:23,010 --> 00:31:24,060
I do.

402
00:31:25,070 --> 00:31:26,630
You'll finish weighing that heart?

403
00:31:28,860 --> 00:31:31,540
That makes you the only person south of the Twins who does.

404
00:31:34,800 --> 00:31:36,950
We're not like the people south of the Twins.

405
00:31:37,800 --> 00:31:40,060
And we're not like the people north of the Twins.

406
00:31:42,130 --> 00:31:46,080
In the Citadel, we lead different lives for different reasons.

407
00:31:47,910 --> 00:31:50,640
We are this world's memory, Samwell Tarly.

408
00:31:50,640 --> 00:31:53,340
Without us, men would be little better than dogs.

409
00:31:53,720 --> 00:31:55,800
Don't remember any meal but the last,

410
00:31:55,810 --> 00:31:58,110
can't see forward to any but the next.

411
00:31:59,010 --> 00:32:00,520
And every time you leave the house and shut the door,

412
00:32:00,530 --> 00:32:02,440
they howl like you're gone forever.

413
00:32:03,760 --> 00:32:05,960
When Robert's Rebellion was raging,

414
00:32:06,770 --> 00:32:08,430
people thought the end was near.

415
00:32:08,430 --> 00:32:11,550
The end of the Targaryen dynasty. "How will we survive?"

416
00:32:11,580 --> 00:32:14,480
When Aegon Targaryen turned his eye westward

417
00:32:15,000 --> 00:32:16,800
and flew his dragons to Blackwater Rush,

418
00:32:16,800 --> 00:32:19,060
"The end is near! How will we survive?"

419
00:32:19,220 --> 00:32:21,750
And thousands of years before that, during the Long Night,

420
00:32:21,750 --> 00:32:23,790
we can forgive them for thinking it truly was the end.

421
00:32:23,790 --> 00:32:26,720
But it wasn't. None of it was.

422
00:32:28,400 --> 00:32:30,760
The Wall has stood through it all.

423
00:32:32,260 --> 00:32:35,030
And every winter that ever came has ended.

424
00:32:43,510 --> 00:32:45,380
Be a good lad. Clean this up.

425
00:33:35,890 --> 00:33:36,800
Nope.

426
00:33:48,140 --> 00:33:49,180
Nope.

427
00:34:01,840 --> 00:34:03,750
You're a lucky man.

428
00:34:08,520 --> 00:34:11,060
I've heard she beat the Hound in single combat.

429
00:34:15,820 --> 00:34:17,590
She's a very impressive woman.

430
00:34:18,720 --> 00:34:20,780
What do you want, Lord Baelish?

431
00:34:24,240 --> 00:34:25,720
I want you to be happy.

432
00:34:26,960 --> 00:34:28,520
I want you to be safe.

433
00:34:28,520 --> 00:34:29,960
I am safe.

434
00:34:30,160 --> 00:34:32,330
I'm at home, surrounded by friends.

435
00:34:33,350 --> 00:34:36,160
I have Brienne to protect me from anyone who would harm me.

436
00:34:40,290 --> 00:34:41,600
What about happy?

437
00:34:44,880 --> 00:34:46,240
Why aren't you happy?

438
00:34:46,770 --> 00:34:48,870
What do you want that you do not have?

439
00:34:48,870 --> 00:34:51,400
At the moment, peace and quiet.

440
00:34:56,660 --> 00:34:59,570
No need to seize the last word, Lord Baelish.

441
00:34:59,760 --> 00:35:01,850
I'll assume it was something clever.

442
00:35:04,400 --> 00:35:05,860
My lady.

443
00:35:06,380 --> 00:35:07,450
My lady.

444
00:35:18,030 --> 00:35:19,630
Why is he still here?

445
00:35:20,630 --> 00:35:22,060
We need his men.

446
00:35:22,720 --> 00:35:23,940
Without the Vale,

447
00:35:23,940 --> 00:35:25,840
Ramsay Bolton would still hold this castle.

448
00:35:27,370 --> 00:35:29,020
Littlefinger saved us.

449
00:35:33,150 --> 00:35:34,500
He wants something.

450
00:35:36,580 --> 00:35:38,860
I know exactly what he wants.

451
00:35:44,070 --> 00:35:47,200
*He rode through the streets of the city*

452
00:35:47,570 --> 00:35:50,610
*Down from his hill on high*

453
00:35:50,690 --> 00:35:53,900
*O'er the winds and the steps and the cobbles*

454
00:35:54,210 --> 00:35:57,160
*He rode to a woman's sigh*

455
00:35:57,730 --> 00:36:00,850
*For she was his secret treasure*

456
00:36:00,960 --> 00:36:03,930
*She was his shame and his bliss*

457
00:36:04,370 --> 00:36:07,280
*And a chain and a keep are nothing*

458
00:36:07,280 --> 00:36:09,950
*Compared to a woman's kiss*

459
00:36:09,950 --> 00:36:13,310
*For hands of gold are always cold*

460
00:36:13,310 --> 00:36:16,380
*But a woman's hands are warm*

461
00:36:16,660 --> 00:36:19,920
*For hands of gold are always cold*

462
00:36:24,320 --> 00:36:25,470
That's a pretty song.

463
00:36:25,790 --> 00:36:27,000
I've never heard it before.

464
00:36:27,000 --> 00:36:28,030
It's a new one.

465
00:36:28,200 --> 00:36:30,630
Are you hungry? We've got some rabbit.

466
00:36:31,400 --> 00:36:32,720
I don't want to steal your food.

467
00:36:32,720 --> 00:36:34,560
You're not stealing, we're offering.

468
00:36:35,300 --> 00:36:37,220
Come on, it's gonna be a cold night.

469
00:37:05,990 --> 00:37:07,130
You heading south?

470
00:37:07,450 --> 00:37:08,450
King's Landing.

471
00:37:09,600 --> 00:37:10,590
Poor girl.

472
00:37:11,890 --> 00:37:13,100
Not so bad, is it?

473
00:37:14,570 --> 00:37:16,340
Depends on your taste, I guess.

474
00:37:16,530 --> 00:37:17,420
If you like your streets covered

475
00:37:17,430 --> 00:37:20,000
in shit and pig's blood, it's the town for you.

476
00:37:20,520 --> 00:37:22,740
All my life, I wanted to see the Red Keep,

477
00:37:22,770 --> 00:37:25,030
the Sept of Baelor, the Dragonpit.

478
00:37:25,030 --> 00:37:26,710
Then when I finally make it,

479
00:37:26,710 --> 00:37:28,690
they wouldn't let me within a mile of the Red Keep,

480
00:37:28,690 --> 00:37:30,850
the Sept of Baelor's blown to hell,

481
00:37:30,940 --> 00:37:33,320
and the Dragonpit is a damn ruin.

482
00:37:33,320 --> 00:37:34,670
The people who live there,

483
00:37:34,720 --> 00:37:35,550
they'd skin you alive if

484
00:37:35,560 --> 00:37:37,440
they could make two coppers off your hide.

485
00:37:37,450 --> 00:37:39,310
Worst place in the world.

486
00:37:39,850 --> 00:37:41,680
What are you doing in the Riverlands?

487
00:37:42,150 --> 00:37:44,710
There's been some trouble with the Freys up at the Twins,

488
00:37:44,710 --> 00:37:48,310
so we're part of the army that's been sent to keep the peace.

489
00:37:51,080 --> 00:37:54,270
Here you go. Guests first.

490
00:37:54,270 --> 00:37:55,970
Oh, no, I couldn't. You don't have enough.

491
00:37:55,970 --> 00:37:58,500
My mother always told me to be kind to strangers.

492
00:37:58,500 --> 00:38:00,350
Strangers will be kind to you.

493
00:38:13,150 --> 00:38:14,720
You're a long way from home.

494
00:38:14,980 --> 00:38:16,970
I'm sure you've had some adventures, though.

495
00:38:16,970 --> 00:38:19,920
Yeah, endless adventures.

496
00:38:20,130 --> 00:38:22,670
They'll be singing about us for a thousand years.

497
00:38:22,670 --> 00:38:26,290
The truth is when we left home, we couldn't wait to get away.

498
00:38:26,290 --> 00:38:28,610
But now we've been gone a while, we can't wait to get home.

499
00:38:28,610 --> 00:38:31,640
I just think about my dad out there on his boat all alone.

500
00:38:32,910 --> 00:38:34,540
I ought to be out there with him.

501
00:38:35,840 --> 00:38:37,850
My wife just had our first baby.

502
00:38:37,850 --> 00:38:40,100
- Boy or girl? - Oh, who knows?

503
00:38:40,100 --> 00:38:42,780
You think soldiers get ravens with news from home?

504
00:38:46,050 --> 00:38:48,860
- I hope it's a girl. - Why?

505
00:38:48,860 --> 00:38:51,850
Girls take care of their papas when their papas grow old.

506
00:38:51,850 --> 00:38:54,490
Boys just go off to fight in someone else's wars.

507
00:38:56,640 --> 00:38:58,400
Are you old enough to drink?

508
00:39:13,760 --> 00:39:15,550
It's blackberry wine.

509
00:39:15,560 --> 00:39:17,360
I made it myself.

510
00:39:18,550 --> 00:39:19,780
It's really good.

511
00:39:21,880 --> 00:39:25,690
So, why is a nice girl on her own heading to King's Landing?

512
00:39:32,690 --> 00:39:34,290
I'm going to kill the queen.

513
00:39:55,980 --> 00:39:58,070
Bad night to be outdoors.

514
00:39:58,070 --> 00:40:01,630
You've got real powerful magic to figure that out.

515
00:40:01,970 --> 00:40:04,870
Did the Lord of Light whisper that in your ear?

516
00:40:04,960 --> 00:40:08,130
"It's snowing, Thoros. It's windy.

517
00:40:08,130 --> 00:40:10,430
It's gonna be a cold night."

518
00:40:11,080 --> 00:40:14,220
You're a grouchy old bear, aren't you, Clegane?

519
00:40:14,790 --> 00:40:16,280
You want some rum?

520
00:40:16,520 --> 00:40:18,920
Don't like that shit. It's too sweet.

521
00:40:19,570 --> 00:40:22,520
Why are you always in such a foul mood?

522
00:40:23,870 --> 00:40:25,900
Experience.

523
00:40:30,430 --> 00:40:32,960
This seems like a good place to spend the night.

524
00:40:35,210 --> 00:40:37,530
These people don't want us here.

525
00:40:37,530 --> 00:40:40,520
Seems deserted to me. No livestock.

526
00:40:40,530 --> 00:40:42,600
No smoke coming from the chimney.

527
00:41:02,040 --> 00:41:03,780
I don't like the look of it.

528
00:41:04,070 --> 00:41:06,570
For a big, hard man, you scare easy.

529
00:41:06,570 --> 00:41:09,000
I'll tell you what doesn't scare me--

530
00:41:09,160 --> 00:41:11,220
bald cocksuckers like you.

531
00:41:11,230 --> 00:41:14,240
You think you're fooling anyone with that top knot?

532
00:41:14,560 --> 00:41:16,140
Bald cunt.

533
00:41:17,790 --> 00:41:18,900
Come on.

534
00:41:19,310 --> 00:41:21,750
Maybe they've got some ale hidden away.

535
00:41:22,720 --> 00:41:24,250
They don't.

536
00:41:27,130 --> 00:41:28,700
See if there's a larder.

537
00:41:28,700 --> 00:41:30,700
They always leave something behind.

538
00:42:12,350 --> 00:42:14,450
How do you think it ended for them?

539
00:42:15,070 --> 00:42:16,670
With death.

540
00:42:16,800 --> 00:42:19,020
Girl died in her father's arms.

541
00:42:19,460 --> 00:42:22,430
Both of them covered in blood and a knife at their feet.

542
00:42:24,630 --> 00:42:26,260
I'd say they were starving.

543
00:42:26,260 --> 00:42:28,410
And rather than let his little girl suffer,

544
00:42:28,410 --> 00:42:30,330
he ended it for both of them.

545
00:42:31,010 --> 00:42:32,420
Doesn't matter now.

546
00:42:32,420 --> 00:42:35,720
No, doesn't matter now.

547
00:42:49,050 --> 00:42:51,710
I've known you a long time, Dondarrion.

548
00:42:51,730 --> 00:42:52,960
Aye.

549
00:42:52,970 --> 00:42:56,850
I think the first time we met was at that tournament--

550
00:42:56,850 --> 00:43:00,870
And I always thought you were dull as dirt.

551
00:43:01,270 --> 00:43:02,760
You're not bad.

552
00:43:03,030 --> 00:43:04,740
I don't hate you.

553
00:43:04,800 --> 00:43:06,920
Don't like you, but you're not bad.

554
00:43:06,920 --> 00:43:08,500
Thank you, Clegane.

555
00:43:08,830 --> 00:43:10,290
That warms the heart.

556
00:43:10,290 --> 00:43:13,210
But there's nothing special about you.

557
00:43:13,620 --> 00:43:15,370
You're right about that.

558
00:43:15,370 --> 00:43:18,880
So why does the Lord of Light keep bringing you back?

559
00:43:19,360 --> 00:43:21,560
I've met better men than you,

560
00:43:21,560 --> 00:43:26,260
and they've been hanged from crossbeams, or beheaded,

561
00:43:26,650 --> 00:43:30,510
or just shat themselves to death in a field somewhere.

562
00:43:31,420 --> 00:43:33,400
None of them came back.

563
00:43:34,790 --> 00:43:36,190
So, why you?

564
00:43:36,230 --> 00:43:38,600
You think I don't ask myself that?

565
00:43:38,870 --> 00:43:41,050
Every hour of every day?

566
00:43:42,010 --> 00:43:43,660
Why am I here?

567
00:43:45,050 --> 00:43:46,830
What am I supposed to do?

568
00:43:46,830 --> 00:43:48,790
What does the Lord see in me?

569
00:43:50,600 --> 00:43:52,010
And?

570
00:43:53,660 --> 00:43:55,200
I don't know.

571
00:43:56,350 --> 00:43:58,370
I don't understand our Lord.

572
00:43:58,370 --> 00:44:00,200
Your Lord.

573
00:44:00,240 --> 00:44:02,220
I don't know what He wants from me.

574
00:44:02,310 --> 00:44:06,700
I only know that He wants me alive.

575
00:44:06,700 --> 00:44:08,230
If he's so all-powerful,

576
00:44:08,240 --> 00:44:11,340
why doesn't he just tell you what the fuck he wants?

577
00:44:12,890 --> 00:44:14,180
Clegane.

578
00:44:14,970 --> 00:44:16,440
Come over here.

579
00:44:18,700 --> 00:44:21,020
Don't worry. The fire won't bite.

580
00:44:22,130 --> 00:44:23,990
I want to show you something.

581
00:44:24,740 --> 00:44:28,650
It's my fucking luck I end up with a band of fire worshippers.

582
00:44:28,900 --> 00:44:30,290
Aye.

583
00:44:30,490 --> 00:44:33,130
Almost seems like divine justice.

584
00:44:33,130 --> 00:44:35,230
There's no divine justice, you dumb cunt.

585
00:44:35,230 --> 00:44:37,260
If there was, you'd be dead...

586
00:44:38,310 --> 00:44:40,790
and that girl would be alive.

587
00:44:46,870 --> 00:44:49,800
- What do you want? - Look into the flames.

588
00:44:49,800 --> 00:44:52,600
I don't want to look in the damn flames.

589
00:44:52,730 --> 00:44:55,760
You saw me bring him back from the dead after you cut him down.

590
00:44:57,050 --> 00:44:59,520
Don't you want to know what gave me the power?

591
00:44:59,520 --> 00:45:02,810
I keep asking and no one wants to tell me.

592
00:45:02,900 --> 00:45:04,550
We can't tell you.

593
00:45:04,570 --> 00:45:06,710
Only the fire can tell you.

594
00:45:19,180 --> 00:45:20,670
What do you see?

595
00:45:22,300 --> 00:45:23,970
Logs burning.

596
00:45:24,540 --> 00:45:26,070
Keep looking.

597
00:45:31,470 --> 00:45:32,980
What do you see?

598
00:45:42,180 --> 00:45:43,640
Ice.

599
00:45:44,850 --> 00:45:46,950
A wall of ice.

600
00:45:49,320 --> 00:45:50,880
The Wall.

601
00:45:53,420 --> 00:45:54,500
What else?

602
00:45:54,510 --> 00:45:58,840
It's where the Wall meets the sea.

603
00:45:59,610 --> 00:46:01,800
There's a castle there.

604
00:46:09,200 --> 00:46:11,390
There's a mountain.

605
00:46:11,650 --> 00:46:13,700
Looks like an arrowhead.

606
00:46:16,940 --> 00:46:19,420
The dead are marching past.

607
00:46:23,890 --> 00:46:25,560
Thousands of them.

608
00:46:31,900 --> 00:46:33,860
Do you believe me now, Clegane?

609
00:46:35,000 --> 00:46:37,150
Do you believe we're here for a reason?

610
00:47:08,630 --> 00:47:10,890
What the hell are you doing, Clegane?

611
00:47:13,650 --> 00:47:15,190
Burying the dead.

612
00:47:28,380 --> 00:47:30,160
You knew these people.

613
00:47:30,510 --> 00:47:32,270
Not really.

614
00:48:32,590 --> 00:48:35,810
We ask the Father to judge us with mercy.

615
00:48:36,470 --> 00:48:39,360
We ask the Mother to...

616
00:48:42,240 --> 00:48:44,760
Fuck it, I don't remember the rest.

617
00:48:50,820 --> 00:48:52,490
I'm sorry you're dead.

618
00:48:53,840 --> 00:48:55,750
You deserved better.

619
00:48:56,790 --> 00:48:58,460
Both of you.

620
00:49:28,710 --> 00:49:29,980
Mom.

621
00:49:30,030 --> 00:49:32,230
You should really sleep, Sam.

622
00:49:33,080 --> 00:49:34,730
The dead don't.

623
00:49:43,610 --> 00:49:47,250
"Legends of the Long Night."

624
00:49:48,920 --> 00:49:52,110
The Targaryens used dragonglass to decorate their weapons

625
00:49:52,110 --> 00:49:55,080
without even knowing what the First Men used it for.

626
00:50:11,990 --> 00:50:13,350
What is it?

627
00:50:14,690 --> 00:50:16,830
It's a map of Dragonstone.

628
00:50:16,830 --> 00:50:19,100
The Targaryens built their first stronghold there

629
00:50:19,100 --> 00:50:20,990
when they invaded Westeros.

630
00:50:23,390 --> 00:50:25,270
That's dragonglass?

631
00:50:25,270 --> 00:50:26,920
A mountain of it.

632
00:50:26,980 --> 00:50:28,250
Beneath the ground.

633
00:50:28,250 --> 00:50:30,470
Stannis told me, but I didn't think...

634
00:50:31,060 --> 00:50:34,410
This is important. Jon needs to know.

635
00:51:27,330 --> 00:51:28,890
Has she come yet?

636
00:51:29,250 --> 00:51:30,460
Who?

637
00:51:30,960 --> 00:51:32,670
The Dragon Queen.

638
00:51:33,250 --> 00:51:35,190
Daenerys Stormborn.

639
00:51:36,960 --> 00:51:38,430
Haven't heard anything.

640
00:57:18,160 --> 00:57:19,580
Shall we begin?

641
00:58:41,320 --> 00:58:43,350
A Targaryen cannot be trusted.

